# 1.1.intake.stone

## .what

capture the raw lesion history verbatim — the person's own words, the lesion timeline, the reported
ABCDE observations, the red-flag symptoms — with no interpretation yet. mark what the case lacks. this
is the ground the compiled route stands on.

## .inputs

- `0.seed.md` — the verbatim input: lesion description, history, location/access constraints

## .do

- transcribe the reported lesion features and timeline exactly as stated
- capture the **ABCDE** observations as reported: Asymmetry, Border, Color, Diameter, Evolution
- capture the **red-flag** symptoms as reported: blood, ulceration, rapid change, itch, a new lesion
  on normal skin, a lesion that stands out from the person's others (the outlier)
- capture **UV / sun-exposure** history (sunburns, indoor-tan-bed use, cumulative outdoor time)
- capture **personal + family melanoma / skin-cancer** history as reported
- note whether a **dermoscopic image** exists, or only a naked-eye / phone photo — the score stone
  needs to know which signal the case carries
- preserve the person's own words for later re-read (do not paraphrase away detail)
- redact identity to a persona handle (`rule.forbid.pii`)
- note the source of each datum (self-reported vs observed vs record), and note each **gap** where a
  datum the score or redteam needs is absent (do not fill a gap by guess)

## .emit

into `1.1.intake.yield.md`.

## .done when

the verbatim lesion history, ABCDE observations, red-flag symptoms, UV history, personal/family
history, timeline, and image-kind are captured, PII-safe, each datum's source marked, each gap noted.
